    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n77002" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰλίωξις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάλι,
		ἰωκή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pursuit in
			turn</i>, when fugitives rally and turn on their pursuers, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. δὲ γένηται ἐκ νηῶν [ῑ</span> metri gr.]
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.71
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄν τοι ἔπειτα π. παρὰ νηῶν αἰὲν
					ἐγὼ τεύχοιμι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.69
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				601
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προΐωξις</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				154
			</span></i>: in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Mith.</u>
				49
			</span></i>.</div>
